# Normalize text files to LF in the repository and working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Common source, docs, and generated data files.
*.cff text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
# Binary assets (never normalize or diff as text).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.bz2 binary
*.sqlite binary
*.ifo binary
*.idx binary
*.dz binary

# --- NUL-carrying documents (H2173 follow-up, 04-08-2026) ---
# These two .md files contain NUL bytes, so git classifies them `-text` regardless of the
# `*.md text eol=lf` rule above: `git add --renormalize` skips them and they read as
# permanently dirty on every checkout, while never matching an `i/crlf|i/mixed` census.
# Declared binary so git's real behaviour is on the books. Removing the NUL bytes would be
# a CONTENT edit to source documents and is deliberately not done here.
literature/md/**/AEK_et_al_corrected_2020.md binary
"literature/md/Lexicography-Manuals/THE ROUTLEDGE HANDBOOK OF HISTORICAL LINGUISTICS.md" binary
